63a6abda-0e05-4c52-9cee-29672a61a296	9baea9f9-4d4c-449d-949c-e5753d4faf67	\N	2	differentiators-section	\N	<section class="differentiators-section" data-component="differentiators">\n        <div class="differentiators-container">\n            <h2>Why Leopardess Consulting</h2>\n            <div class="differentiators-grid">\n                \n                <div class="differentiator-item">\n                    <h3>We Build, We Don't Just Advise</h3>\n                    <p>We are practitioners first. Every recommendation we make is grounded in systems we have actually designed, deployed, and run in production. When we talk about multi-agent orchestration, we mean working pipelines – not whitepapers.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class="differentiator-item">\n                    <h3>Speed Without Shortcuts</h3>\n                    <p>Our automated deployment pipelines get production-ready websites and agent systems live in minutes rather than weeks. Fast delivery does not mean fragile delivery – security, testing, and reliability are built into every step.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class="differentiator-item">\n                    <h3>A Stack Built for the Real World</h3>\n                    <p>We work with Kubernetes, Kafka, and Postgres because they are proven at scale. This is not a trend-chasing technology choice – it is a deliberate foundation that gives your systems the resilience and throughput enterprise workloads demand.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class="differentiator-item">\n                    <h3>Hierarchical Multi-Agent Expertise</h3>\n                    <p>Designing agent systems that actually collaborate requires more than wiring together API calls. We architect hierarchical structures where agents delegate intelligently, share context in real time, and recover gracefully when things go wrong.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class="differentiator-item">\n                    <h3>Cloudflare-Native Deployment</h3>\n                    <p>Our web automation practice is built around Cloudflare's global network, giving your applications edge-level performance, DDoS protection, and automated build and launch workflows out of the box – without the usual infrastructure overhead.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class="differentiator-item">\n                    <h3>Practical AI Adoption, Not Hype</h3>\n                    <p>We help technology leaders make clear-headed decisions about where AI actually adds value in their operations. Our roadmaps are grounded in your existing workflows and constraints – built to deliver measurable progress, not impressive slide decks.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </section>\n<style>\n.differentiators-section {\n    padding: var(--spacing-section, 5rem 2rem);\n    background: var(--color-background, #fff);\n}\n.differentiators-container {\n    max-width: var(--container-max-width, 1200px);\n    margin: 0 auto;\n}\n.differentiators-section h2 {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);\n    margin-bottom: 3rem;\n    color: var(--color-primary, #1a1a2e);\n}\n.differentiators-grid {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));\n    gap: 2rem;\n}\n.differentiator-item {\n    padding: 2rem;\n    background: var(--color-surface, #f8f9fa);\n    border-radius: 8px;\n    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent, #0f3460);\n}\n.differentiator-item h3 {\n    font-size: 1.25rem;\n    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n    color: var(--color-primary, #1a1a2e);\n}\n.differentiator-item p {\n    color: var(--color-text-muted, #555);\n    line-height: 1.7;\n    margin: 0;\n}\n@media (max-width: 768px) {\n    .differentiators-section { padding: 3rem 1.5rem; }\n    .differentiators-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n}\n</style>	\N	\N	\N	1c324e19-b025-4abb-8dc9-a24a9664c0e7	2026-03-09 18:28:10.914316+00	2026-03-09 18:28:10.914316+00	deployed	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
c3c4ab63-e791-42db-b853-3b695c432eb6	9baea9f9-4d4c-449d-949c-e5753d4faf67	\N	3	features	\N	<section class="features-section" data-component="features">\n    <div class="features-container">\n        <h2>Built to Run. Designed to Scale.</h2>\n        <p class="features-subtitle">From hierarchical agent architectures to production deployments, every system we build is engineered to work reliably in the real world — not just in demos.</p>\n        <div class="features-grid">\n            \n            <div class="feature-item">\n                <div class="feature-icon"><i data-lucide="network"></i></div>\n                <h3>Hierarchical Multi-Agent Orchestration</h3>\n                <p>We design and deploy multi-agent systems where tasks are intelligently delegated across specialised agents. Each layer of the hierarchy knows its role — coordinating, executing, and reporting — so complex workflows complete without bottlenecks or human hand-holding.</p>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class="feature-item">\n                <div class="feature-icon"><i data-lucide="rocket"></i></div>\n                <h3>Automated Website Deployment</h3>\n                <p>Production-ready websites go live in minutes, not weeks. Our AI-powered pipelines handle the full build, test, and launch sequence on Cloudflare's infrastructure — secure, fast, and repeatable from day one.</p>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class="feature-item">\n                <div class="feature-icon"><i data-lucide="server"></i></div>\n                <h3>Proven Enterprise Stack</h3>\n                <p>Every system runs on a battle-tested foundation: Kubernetes for container orchestration, Kafka for real-time event streaming, and Postgres for reliable data persistence. No experimental infrastructure — just solid components that hold up under production load.</p>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class="feature-item">\n                <div class="feature-icon"><i data-lucide="cpu"></i></div>\n                <h3>Multi-Model LLM Support</h3>\n                <p>Our agent systems are model-agnostic by design. Whether your workflow calls for GPT-4, Claude, Mistral, or a fine-tuned specialist model, we configure the right LLM for each task — and swap or upgrade without rebuilding from scratch.</p>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class="feature-item">\n                <div class="feature-icon"><i data-lucide="shield"></i></div>\n                <h3>Security and Reliability by Default</h3>\n                <p>Enterprise-grade security isn't an add-on here — it's baked into the architecture. Automated testing, controlled deployments, and Cloudflare's edge network mean your systems stay available, auditable, and protected.</p>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class="feature-item">\n                <div class="feature-icon"><i data-lucide="map"></i></div>\n                <h3>Digital Transformation Roadmapping</h3>\n                <p>We work directly with your team to identify where AI and automation create genuine value. You get a clear, practical adoption plan — not a theoretical framework — built around your existing workflows and realistic timelines.</p>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class="feature-item">\n                <div class="feature-icon"><i data-lucide="git-branch"></i></div>\n                <h3>Real-Time Agent Collaboration</h3>\n                <p>Agents in our systems don't operate in isolation. They communicate, share context, and hand off tasks in real time — enabling workflows that adapt dynamically as conditions change, rather than following rigid pre-scripted paths.</p>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class="feature-item">\n                <div class="feature-icon"><i data-lucide="trending-up"></i></div>\n                <h3>Systems That Scale With You</h3>\n                <p>Whether you're automating a single workflow or orchestrating dozens of concurrent agent pipelines, the architecture scales horizontally. Start focused, expand deliberately — without re-engineering what already works.</p>\n            </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>\n<style>\n/* Layout only - colors inherited from global CSS */\n.features-section {\n    padding: var(--spacing-section, 5rem 2rem);\n}\n.features-container {\n    max-width: var(--container-max-width, 1200px);\n    margin: 0 auto;\n}\n.features-section h2 {\n    text-align: center;\n    margin-bottom: 1rem;\n}\n.features-subtitle {\n    text-align: center;\n    max-width: 600px;\n    margin: 0 auto 3rem;\n}\n.features-grid {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));\n    gap: 2rem;\n}\n.feature-item {\n    text-align: center;\n    padding: 2rem;\n}\n.feature-icon {\n    width: 48px;\n    height: 48px;\n    margin: 0 auto 1rem;\n    color: var(--color-accent, #0f3460);\n}\n.feature-icon svg {\n    width: 100%;\n    height: 100%;\n}\n.feature-item h3 {\n    margin-bottom: 1rem;\n}\n.feature-item p {\n    margin: 0;\n}\n@media (max-width: 768px) {\n    .features-section { padding: 3rem 1.5rem; }\n    .features-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }\n}\n</style>	\N	\N	\N	ede6818c-ff87-4c89-8c32-2758ee40bfd0	2026-03-09 18:28:10.919495+00	2026-03-09 18:28:10.919495+00	deployed	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
202f1c94-e96d-4315-b2a6-2d7634b11e2c	9baea9f9-4d4c-449d-949c-e5753d4faf67	\N	4	case-studies-list	\N	<section class="case-studies-section" data-component="case-studies-list">\n    <div class="case-studies-container">\n        <h2>Systems That Work in the Real World</h2>\n        <p class="case-studies-subtitle">We build and deploy production-grade AI agent systems. Here is the kind of work we do and what it looks like when it runs.</p>\n        <div class="case-studies-grid">\n            \n            <article class="case-study-item">\n                <h3>Automated Website Deployment Pipeline</h3>\n                <p class="case-study-client">Web-first businesses and growing tech teams</p>\n                <p>Many teams spend weeks getting a new web property from brief to live deployment — navigating CI/CD configuration, hosting setup, security hardening, and testing cycles. We replace that process with a multi-agent pipeline that handles automated builds, testing, and Cloudflare deployment in a single coordinated workflow. Agents manage each stage independently, flag issues before they reach production, and hand off cleanly between tasks without human bottlenecks.</p>\n                <p class="case-study-results"><strong>Results:</strong> Teams move from brief to production-ready deployment in a fraction of the usual time. The pipeline runs consistently, catches errors early, and removes the manual overhead that typically slows launches down.</p>\n            </article>\n            \n            <article class="case-study-item">\n                <h3>Hierarchical Multi-Agent Orchestration</h3>\n                <p class="case-study-client">CTOs and engineering leads managing complex automation requirements</p>\n                <p>Businesses with layered workflows — where tasks depend on each other, require different models, or need to scale unpredictably — often find that single-agent or rigid automation tools fall short. We design hierarchical agent systems where a coordinating layer delegates to specialised sub-agents, each handling a defined scope. Built on Kubernetes for resilience, Kafka for real-time event handling, and Postgres for reliable state management, these systems are built to run under production conditions, not just in demos.</p>\n                <p class="case-study-results"><strong>Results:</strong> Workflows that previously required constant human intervention run autonomously and reliably. The architecture scales cleanly under load and supports multiple LLMs and models without requiring a rebuild when requirements change.</p>\n            </article>\n            \n            <article class="case-study-item">\n                <h3>Digital Transformation Roadmapping</h3>\n                <p class="case-study-client">Established businesses beginning structured AI adoption</p>\n                <p>Organisations that recognise the need to modernise their operations often lack a clear, practical path to get there. We work directly with leadership teams to map existing workflows, identify where AI agents and automation deliver genuine value, and build a sequenced adoption plan that does not require disrupting everything at once. The focus is on decisions that can be implemented, not frameworks that sit in a slide deck.</p>\n                <p class="case-study-results"><strong>Results:</strong> Leadership teams leave with a concrete plan they can act on, with clear priorities and realistic timelines. Early implementation phases typically surface quick wins that build internal confidence for broader rollout.</p>\n            </article>\n            \n            <article class="case-study-item">\n                <h3>Web Architecture and AI Integration Consultancy</h3>\n                <p class="case-study-client">Development teams building or modernising web applications</p>\n                <p>Engineering teams building modern web applications frequently face decisions around architecture, deployment strategy, and where AI capabilities add real value versus where they add complexity. We work alongside these teams to review current approaches, recommend practical improvements, and help integrate AI tooling — whether that is intelligent content workflows, automated quality checks, or agent-assisted user experiences — in ways that fit the existing stack and team capability.</p>\n                <p class="case-study-results"><strong>Results:</strong> Teams gain clarity on architectural decisions that will hold up as requirements grow. Integrations are scoped to what is genuinely useful, reducing the risk of over-engineering and keeping delivery timelines on track.</p>\n            </article>\n            \n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>\n<style>\n/* Layout only - colors inherited from global CSS */\n.case-studies-section {\n    padding: var(--spacing-section, 5rem 2rem);\n    background: var(--color-surface, #f8f9fa);\n}\n.case-studies-container {\n    max-width: var(--container-max-width, 1200px);\n    margin: 0 auto;\n}\n.case-studies-section h2 {\n    text-align: center;\n    margin-bottom: 1rem;\n}\n.case-studies-subtitle {\n    text-align: center;\n    max-width: 600px;\n    margin: 0 auto 3rem;\n}\n.case-studies-grid {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));\n    gap: 2rem;\n}\n.case-study-item {\n    padding: 2rem;\n    background: var(--color-background, #fff);\n    border-radius: 8px;\n    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);\n}\n.case-study-item h3 {\n    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n}\n.case-study-client {\n    font-size: 0.9rem;\n    margin-bottom: 1rem;\n    color: var(--color-text-muted, #666);\n}\n.case-study-results {\n    margin-top: 1rem;\n    padding-top: 1rem;\n    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border, #e2e8f0);\n}\n@media (max-width: 768px) {\n    .case-studies-section { padding: 3rem 1.5rem; }\n    .case-studies-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n}\n</style>	\N	\N	\N	dcc3969f-e0fe-4b5f-ac58-bb9c0a3