f696c1a5-23a9-4d7f-afc0-50b4411a67e6	628106db-5501-449c-aa64-1bb4dcc55c98	0806d841-3bea-46d9-ab33-a18c01771e45	1	hero-case-studies	\N	<section class="hero hero-case-studies" data-component="hero-case-studies">\n        <div class="hero-content">\n            <h1>Real Systems. Real Scale. Real Production.</h1>\n            <p class="hero-subheadline">How engineering teams are building reliable multi-agent systems that handle millions of tasks, recover from failures, and scale with their business.</p>\n        </div>\n    </section>\n<style>\n.hero-case-studies {\n    min-height: 50vh;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    text-align: center;\n    padding: 4rem 2rem;\n    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #16213e 50%, #0f3460 100%);\n\n    /* Dark section context */\n    --section-text: rgba(255,255,255,0.9);\n    --section-text-muted: rgba(255,255,255,0.7);\n    --section-heading: #ffffff;\n    --section-surface: rgba(255,255,255,0.05);\n    --section-border: rgba(255,255,255,0.2);\n}\n.hero-case-studies .hero-content {\n    max-width: 800px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    color: #fff;\n}\n.hero-case-studies h1 {\n    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);\n    font-weight: 700;\n    margin-bottom: 1rem;\n    line-height: 1.2;\n}\n.hero-case-studies .hero-subheadline {\n    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.2rem);\n    line-height: 1.6;\n}\n</style>	\N	\N	\N	891bdafc-58f8-45f5-988b-c6abb653bae9	2026-02-22 18:43:33.912922+00	2026-02-22 18:43:33.912922+00	deployed	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
3ec51ddc-9010-43d5-a3cb-1cc9b4b8a625	628106db-5501-449c-aa64-1bb4dcc55c98	e7fc34f7-ef74-4665-830d-2c130c689002	2	case-studies-list	\N	<section class="case-studies-section" data-component="case-studies-list">\n    <div class="case-studies-container">\n        <h2>Production Agent Systems That Actually Ship</h2>\n        <p class="case-studies-subtitle">Real-world architectures solving distributed orchestration, state management, and observability at scale</p>\n        <div class="case-studies-grid">\n            \n            <article class="case-study-item">\n                <h3>Multi-Stage Document Processing Pipeline</h3>\n                <p class="case-study-client">Document Intelligence Systems</p>\n                <p>Hierarchical agent architecture coordinating extraction, validation, and enrichment workflows across heterogeneous document types with HITL approval gates for quality control.</p>\n                <p class="case-study-results"><strong>Results:</strong> Saga-based error recovery handles partial failures across 12+ processing steps. Kafka message isolation prevents cross-document state pollution. Correlation IDs trace documents through the entire pipeline with step-level observability.</p>\n            </article>\n            \n            <article class="case-study-item">\n                <h3>Adaptive Research & Analysis Workflow</h3>\n                <p class="case-study-client">Knowledge Synthesis Platform</p>\n                <p>Parent agents dynamically spawn specialist sub-agents for web research, data extraction, and synthesis. LLM integration with structured prompt templates feeds collected context into analysis steps.</p>\n                <p class="case-study-results"><strong>Results:</strong> Declarative workflow graphs with branching logic handle research path variations. Retry with exponential backoff manages LLM rate limits and transient failures. Full execution traces enable debugging of multi-agent reasoning chains.</p>\n            </article>\n            \n            <article class="case-study-item">\n                <h3>Customer Support Triage & Routing</h3>\n                <p class="case-study-client">Support Automation Infrastructure</p>\n                <p>Request-response messaging patterns route support tickets to specialized agents based on classification results. HITL gates escalate edge cases to human operators with full context preservation.</p>\n                <p class="case-study-results"><strong>Results:</strong> Fan-out broadcasts distribute tickets to multiple classifiers in parallel. Saga coordination ensures tickets reach resolution even when individual agents timeout. Structured logging captures decision rationale for compliance audits.</p>\n            </article>\n            \n            <article class="case-study-item">\n                <h3>Compliance Review & Approval System</h3>\n                <p class="case-study-client">Regulated Content Platform</p>\n                <p>Multi-stage approval workflow with configurable HITL checkpoints. Agents pause execution at review gates, maintain distributed state during human review cycles, and resume processing on approval.</p>\n                <p class="case-study-results"><strong>Results:</strong> Timeout handling with auto-escalation prevents stalled workflows. Kafka topic isolation separates review queues by priority and content type. Audit trail captures every state transition with timestamp and approver metadata.</p>\n            </article>\n            \n            <article class="case-study-item">\n                <h3>Data Pipeline Orchestration</h3>\n                <p class="case-study-client">ETL & Transformation Infrastructure</p>\n                <p>Workflow engine coordinates extract, transform, and load operations across multiple data sources. Error recovery handles partial batch failures without reprocessing successful records.</p>\n                <p class="case-study-results"><strong>Results:</strong> Declarative step graphs define complex dependency chains with conditional execution. Distributed state management tracks progress across long-running transformations. Replayable message flows enable recovery from infrastructure failures.</p>\n            </article>\n            \n            <article class="case-study-item">\n                <h3>Content Generation & Review Pipeline</h3>\n                <p class="case-study-client">Publishing Workflow System</p>\n                <p>LLM-powered content generation integrated into approval workflows. Agents coordinate draft creation, fact-checking, style validation, and editorial review with structured handoffs between automated and human steps.</p>\n                <p class="case-study-results"><strong>Results:</strong> Variable injection from collected data feeds context into LLM prompts. Same retry logic and error handling applies to LLM calls as any other action. Trace files capture prompt-response pairs for quality analysis and prompt tuning.</p>\n            </article>\n            \n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>\n<style>\n/* Layout only - colors inherited from global CSS */\n.case-studies-section {\n    padding: var(--spacing-section, 5rem 2rem);\n    background: var(--color-surface, #f8f9fa);\n}\n.case-studies-container {\n    max-width: var(--container-max-width, 1200px);\n    margin: 0 auto;\n}\n.case-studies-section h2 {\n    text-align: center;\n    margin-bottom: 1rem;\n}\n.case-studies-subtitle {\n    text-align: center;\n    max-width: 600px;\n    margin: 0 auto 3rem;\n}\n.case-studies-grid {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));\n    gap: 2rem;\n}\n.case-study-item {\n    padding: 2rem;\n    background: var(--color-background, #fff);\n    border-radius: 8px;\n    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);\n}\n.case-study-item h3 {\n    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n}\n.case-study-client {\n    font-size: 0.9rem;\n    margin-bottom: 1rem;\n    color: var(--color-text-muted, #666);\n}\n.case-study-results {\n    margin-top: 1rem;\n    padding-top: 1rem;\n    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border, #e2e8f0);\n}\n@media (max-width: 768px) {\n    .case-studies-section { padding: 3rem 1.5rem; }\n    .case-studies-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n}\n</style>	\N	\N	\N	821a4c32-27f4-4362-8611-d2e5effa4237	2026-02-22 18:43:33.918233+00	2026-02-22 18:43:33.918233+00	deployed	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
